sess38 precedent).
GPT ruling (gpt-5.6-sol, this sess): per-I/O ctx->lock scope; separate
holds for read vs CAW; new local ctx->purge_lock held across whole purge
(hb NEVER takes it; order purge_lock -> ctx->lock, never reverse);
amortized (~2s elapsed) authority revalidation mid-scan via the phase-0
gate sector; preserve P235 probes; per-sector not batched.
ALREADY EDITED (in tree, uncompiled): disklock.h purge_lock field;
disklock.c create/destroy of purge_lock; new purge_recov_gate() helper
factored out, purge_hb_zeroable now calls it (semantics unchanged).
REMAINING EDIT: restructure mxfs_disklock_purge_node itself —
  - take purge_lock at entry, drop the long ctx->lock hold;
  - per-I/O ctx->lock around: phase-0 gate reads, main-loop read_sector,
    each purge_cas_zero, CAS-retry re-reads, HB-scan reads + CAS;
  - phase 0: use purge_recov_gate (remember gate_off + gate_found when
    it returns 0); refusal path unlocks purge_lock;
  - main loop: if gate_found and >2000ms since last check, re-read
    gate_off under ctx->lock, purge_recov_gate again: -ENOENT => consumed
    elsewhere, set gate_found=false and continue; refusal => log
    P234-PURGE-REFROZE-MIDSCAN (purged-so-far), cleanup, return rc;
  - final unlock is purge_lock (ctx->lock no longer held there).
